Michael Finley as Bart Millard, the lead singer who wrote the song
about his relationship with his father (Dennis Quaid).

15
01:11:44,347 --> 01:11:50,347
Madeline Carroll, Trace Adkins, Priscilla Shirer, and Cloris Leachman also star.

16
01:16:31,304 --> 01:16:37,304
I Can Only Imagine was released in the United States on March 16, 2018.

17
01:21:18,260 --> 01:21:24,260
It was a box office success, grossing $86 million worldwide against a production
budget of $7 million, earning more than twelve times its budget.

18
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
It is the fifth highest-grossing music biopic and sixth
highest-grossing Christian film of all-time in the United States.

19
01:30:52,173 --> 01:30:58,173
Some critics praised it as inspiring and noted it as an improvement compared to other
faith-based films, while others called it flat and by-the-numbers.

20
01:35:39,130 --> 01:35:45,130
At the 2018 Dove Awards, the film won "Inspirational Film of the Year".

21
